      "title": "JEE Main 2023 (29 Jan Shift 2)"
    }
  ],
  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be a relation defined on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi></math> as a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> b is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></math> is a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NDkgt",
      "text": "not reflexive",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xDZVX",
      "text": "transitive but not symmetric",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ghjhl",
      "text": "symmetric but not transitive",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Hvfsj",
      "text": "an equivalence relation",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>divisible</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>by</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>for</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><strong>Reflexive:</strong></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is always divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><strong>Symmetric:</strong></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>.</p><p>Now,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>multiple</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>multiple</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>multiple</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>multiple</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><strong>Transitive:</strong></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p><p>So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is an equivalence relation.</p>",
